WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Sam wants to say "I will speak".

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.150
He starts from the verb hablar,

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.750
and he knows the
future ending for "I".

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.790
So he does what he always does.

5
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.830
He chops off the old ending
and adds the new one.

6
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.430
He gets: hablé.

7
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.480
But that word already means "I spoke"!

8
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.890
He's landed in the wrong tense.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.370
So where should the ending really go?

10
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.610
In this mission, you'll learn
the endings of the simple future,

11
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.930
and the endings of the conditional,
the tense for "would".

12
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.450
You'll find the trick
the two tenses share,

13
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.230
and meet verbs like tener
and hacer with special stems.

14
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.190
Your mission: work out where
the future endings really go.
